{
  "key": "pr-1105",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "fix(release): label auto-release PRs chore:pin — ride the machine fast-lane",
    "description": "Release bump PRs (`chore(release): vX`) are machine-generated one-purpose changes; routing them through the full LLM review chain wastes a review cycle (~15-25 min + tokens) on a pubspec/CHANGELOG bump. Factory-pin PRs already carry `chore:pin`, which the SM exempts from the review lane and the gate bridge (#847/#848) — release PRs are the same class.\n\n- `gh pr create` gains `--label chore:pin`\n- the refresh path re-applies the label on already-open release PRs (covers PRs opened before this fix, e.g. #1104, which I labeled manually)\n\nRefs #1098, #1093."
  }
}

